hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19176","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Aqil, judge of Wasit, from Sabiq ibn Najiya, from Abu Sallam, he said: A man passed in the mosque of Hims, and they said: This is a servant of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I stood to him and said: Tell me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which men do not pass between you and him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim servant says when he mornings and when he evenings three times: I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Prophet, but it is a right upon Allah to please him on the Day of Resurrection."
"19177","Waki narrated to us: Misar narrated to us, from Abu Aqil, from Sabiq, from Abu Sallam, from a servant of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever says: I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet, when he evenings three times and when he mornings three times, it is a right upon Allah to please him on the Day of Resurrection."
"19178","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Aqil Hashim ibn Bilal, from Sabiq ibn Najiya, from Abu Sallam. Abu al-Nadr al-Habashi said: A man passed by him in the mosque of Hims, and it was said: This served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he stood to him and said: Tell me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which men did not pass between you and him. He said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No servant says when he evenings and when he mornings: I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Prophet, three times, but it is a right upon Allah to please him."
"19179","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us: Rushdin ibn Sad narrated to us: Bakr ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Hubayra, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, that a man who served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eight years narrated to him, he said: When food was brought near to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: In the name of Allah. Then when he finished his food he said: O Allah, You fed and gave drink and enriched and sufficed and guided and chose; to You is praise for what You gave."
